{"Upsampling cache key uses Python hash() which is process-randomized, making cached eligibility inconsistent between processes and causing cache invalidation via invalidate_upsampling_cache() to miss entries created by different processes": 0.9806951284408569, "Upsampling eligibility is computed before dashboard split logic and can use the wrong dataset - should_upsample is calculated from outer dataset before get_event_stats_factory() handles metrics-enhanced dashboard split path, causing brittle coupling between Discover and Errors routing": 0.490266352891922, "upsampled_count() aggregate is only registered in Discover's SnQL function converter but endpoint rewrites count() to upsampled_count() across RPC and non-RPC paths, causing failures when transformed function reaches unsupported dataset/path": 0.9113956093788147, "Event factory mutates every event with truthy client_sample_rate even when invalid, swallowing all exceptions and silently converting bad fixture data which can mask test failures": 0.5083758234977722, "Factory mutation rewrites normalized_data in place and can leak sample_rate into callers that reuse the dict, affecting any caller that reuses dict after store_event() returns": 0.7551311254501343}